  // AFTER ms after the last lift. Touch / wheel, not 'scroll': a scroll listener anywhere (even passive) makes Chromium run
  // a main-thread frame for every scrolled frame of every scroller (PAGES, 1 Nov); without one, scrolling stays on the
  // compositor. A finger held still for 8 s no longer holds the clock (a lost touchend cannot stop it).
  // 0.10.4 ZEROJS: + the tab bar: a tab tap switches pages (the strip jumps, the switch runs in idle): no tick in those frames
